{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"bf99a9cd-1d83-4081-a775-31cecc85a336","title":"The normal distribution and the 68-95-99.7 rule"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bf99a9cd-1d83-4081-a775-31cecc85a336","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A normal distribution is a symmetric bell curve. Its center is the mean, μ, and its spread is measured by the standard deviation, σ.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"The normal distribution"},{"op":"equation","id":"standardize","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"z=\\frac{x-\\mu}{\\sigma}"},{"op":"figure","id":"bell","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-4,4],"y":[0,0.45],"axes":"edge","x_label":"z (standard deviations)","y_label":"Probability density"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"density","y":"exp(-x^2/2)/sqrt(2*pi)","domain":[-4,4]},{"kind":"segment","from":[0,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":0},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[0,0.425],"text":"mean","size":"small"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bf99a9cd-1d83-4081-a775-31cecc85a336","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Probability is area under the curve. About 68 percent of observations lie within one standard deviation of the mean.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"band_one","on":"bell","marks":[{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":-1,"to":1},{"kind":"point","at":{"on":"density","x":-1},"label":"−1σ"},{"kind":"point","at":{"on":"density","x":1},"label":"+1σ"},{"kind":"text","at":[0,0.13],"text":"68%"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule_one","anchor":{"el":"standardize","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(\\mu-\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+\\sigma)\\approx68\\%"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bf99a9cd-1d83-4081-a775-31cecc85a336","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Expanding to two standard deviations captures about 95 percent. Each newly included side contributes roughly 13.5 percent.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"band_two","on":"bell","marks":[{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":-2,"to":-1},{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":1,"to":2},{"kind":"point","at":{"on":"density","x":-2},"label":"−2σ"},{"kind":"point","at":{"on":"density","x":2},"label":"+2σ"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule_two","anchor":{"el":"rule_one","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(\\mu-2\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+2\\sigma)\\approx95\\%"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bf99a9cd-1d83-4081-a775-31cecc85a336","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Within three standard deviations lies about 99.7 percent. Only 0.3 percent remains outside, split equally between the two tails. These percentages apply to normal distributions.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"band_three","on":"bell","marks":[{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":-3,"to":-2},{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":2,"to":3},{"kind":"segment","from":[-3,0],"to":[-3,0.04],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":[3,0],"to":[3,0.04],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[-3,0.065],"text":"−3σ","size":"small"},{"kind":"text","at":[3,0.065],"text":"+3σ","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule_three","anchor":{"el":"rule_two","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(\\mu-3\\sigma\\le X\\le\\mu+3\\sigma)\\approx99.7\\%"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"About what percentage lies more than three standard deviations above the mean?","expected_gist":"0.15%, half of the remaining 0.3%"}}}
